Context
Repo: https://github.com/olenapetrova-da/lublin-events-hub
Release: v0.3.0-rc.3
Task: #3 Implement doGet(e) Query API (Apps Script)

Goal / DoD
- Serve JSON from the normalized `events` sheet, but include **display fields** that users see:
  • `date` (YYYY-MM-DD),  • `times` (comma string from raw_events),
  • plus title, payment, categories, venue, url, source.
- Use `events.start_dt/end_dt` only for logic (range overlap, DST-safe sorting).
- Sorting: per ADR-0011 — timed first → date asc → earliest time asc → title asc.
- JSON contract stable; CORS; clear 400/500 errors; 5 smoke tests.
- Daily automation (OPS-TR1) already runs refresh+materialize; `doGet` reads the **fresh `events`**.
- On exception: email Script Property `ALERT_EMAIL`.

Dependencies (assume done)
- `materialize()` implemented (events columns below)
- Script Properties: `SHEET_ID`, `TZ="Europe/Warsaw"`, `ALERT_EMAIL` (optional)
- Web App deployment will be done after code is ready

Input sheets
- `events` (9 cols): event_id | title | start_dt | end_dt | venue | payment | categories | source | url
- `raw_events` (9 cols): Title | Date | Time | Venue | Category | Link | Payment for Entry | Source | _EndDate
- `taxonomy_alias` (alias, canonical) — used to map request categories to canonical for filtering

API — Request (query params)
- date: YYYY-MM-DD (required unless start+end provided)
- period: day|week|range|weekend (default: day)
- days: int (used only if period=range and start/end not provided)
- start, end: YYYY-MM-DD (explicit window; when both present, ignore period/days)
- payment: any|free|paid|unknown (default any)
- category: comma list; map via taxonomy_alias → canonical; match if any present in event’s pipe-joined categories
- source: optional filter (comma list of hostnames)
- limit: int (default 20, max 100)
- offset: int (default 0)
- tz: optional override for formatting if ever needed (default Script Property TZ)

API — Response (JSON)
{
  "ok": true,
  "start": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "end": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "total": <int>,            // matches BEFORE pagination
  "limit": <int>,
  "offset": <int>,
  "next_offset": <int|null>,
  "results": [
    {
      // DISPLAY FIELDS (for users/bot)
      "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
      "title": "...",
      "times": "09:30, 11:30",
      "payment": "free|paid|unknown",
      "categories": "kids|music",
      "venue": "...",
      "source": "zoom.lublin.pl",
      "url": "https://...",

      // TECH FIELDS (useful to clients; not required for display)
      "event_id": "...",
      "start_dt": "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS+01:00",
      "end_dt":   "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS+01:00"
    }
  ]
}

Required behaviors
- Window:
  • period=day → [date,date]
  • period=week → [date,date+6]
  • period=weekend → Sat/Sun window that contains `date`
  • period=range or (start&end) → use explicit
- Load:
  • Read all rows from `events` once.
  • Build an index from `raw_events` to supply `times` by key `(Source, Link, Date)` (case-sensitive on URL host; Date ISO).
- Filtering:
  • Overlap rule: include if `event.end_dt_date >= start && event.start_dt_date <= end` (date parts only).
  • Apply `payment` unless `any`.
  • Map request `category` via `taxonomy_alias` → canonical; keep event if any requested canonical is contained in event’s pipe-joined `categories`.
  • Apply `source` filter if provided.
- Sorting (ADR-0011):
  1) **timed first** — treat as “timed” if the time portion of `start_dt` is not `00:00:00`
  2) by **date** (YYYY-MM-DD from `start_dt`)
  3) by **time** (HH:MM from `start_dt`) for timed items
  4) by **title** A→Z (Polish locale, case-insensitive)
- Pagination: slice by limit/offset; `next_offset = (offset+limit < total ? offset+limit : null)`.
- Response fields exactly as shown. Include CORS header `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`.
- Logging: one line per request, e.g.  
  `doGet window=YYYY-MM-DD..YYYY-MM-DD, pay=any, cat=[kids], src=[], total=42, page=20/0`
- On exception: return `{ok:false, error:"..."}` with HTTP 500 and send an email to `ALERT_EMAIL` if set.

